All clients are affected. The problem is `useExportCsv` doesn't re-register when `getRows` changes.

Now let me also verify by reading the source carefully:

Looking at the hook: `register(pathname, serializer)` runs in useEffect. The serializer captures `opts`. But useEffect only re-runs on `[pathname, register, unregister]`. When `data` updates → render → new `opts` → new `getRows` → but the OLD serializer is still in the registry.

Actually wait — let me think about this differently. The hook signature:

```ts
export function useExportCsv<T>(opts: UseExportCsvOptions<T>): void {
  // ...
  useEffect(() => {
    const serializer = async (rangeLabel) => {
      const rows = await opts.getRows()  // <-- captures opts
      ...
    }
    register(pathname, serializer)
    return () => unregister(pathname)
  }, [pathname, register, unregister])
}
```

When the component re-renders with new `opts` (new `getRows` reference but same data behind it), the hook is called again. But the useEffect doesn't depend on `opts`, so it doesn't re-run. The `serializer` previously registered captures the FIRST `opts`. So yes, stale.

